    "title": "High winds knock down scoreboard at Cave Spring Middle School - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Dawn Forrest ,\n1 hours ago\nROANOKE, Va. ( WFXR ) – High winds tore through the Roanoke Valley as a storm front stalled over the region.\nPinpoint Weather: Turning cooler as rain chances continue Over at Cave Spring Middle School, the rough weather caused the Bogle Stadium scoreboard to topple over last night, May 20.\nA girls lacrosse game was scheduled between Cave Spring and Patrick Henry at the stadium.\nNo one was hurt or on the field at the time of the fall, school officials say.\nSchool officials and the scoreboard makers will arrive at the stadium today, May 21, to check the damage.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WFXRtv.",
    "summary": "Pinpoint Weather: Turning cooler as rain chances continue Over at Cave Spring Middle School, the rough weather caused the Bogle Stadium scoreboard to topple over last night, May 20. A girls lacrosse game was scheduled between Cave Spring and Patrick Henry at the stadium. No one was hurt or on the field at the time of the fall, school officials say. School officials and the scoreboard makers will arrive at the stadium today, May 21, to check the damage. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WFXRtv.",
